How's this for an idea. The latest fad in programming nowadays seems to 
be making bots that learn how to do stuff by themselves by simply 
letting them apply random output to a system, and whichever random 
output has the best effect on the system, use that as a launching point 
for the next iteration, etc, a sort of evolutionary model.

So why not toss one of these "learnng models" into nethack and let it 
run around for a while, using the score when it dies as the basis for 
judging how well it's doing. A few conditionals to let it know the 
special significance of stuff like the Amulet of Yendor and ascending, 
and you're all set.

I am not a programmer, so feel free to flame me if I'm completely wrong. 
The one thing I can see is that the database would get huge, so the bot 
wouldn't exactly be portable.

